    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "46cadc45-63ea-3c6a-9768-6f09e06a878c",
                "word": "dominical",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f632291e-e7cd-3c4f-bbba-f33d14411554",
                        "entry_id": "46cadc45-63ea-3c6a-9768-6f09e06a878c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to Jesus Christ as Lord."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3fe72c5b-9b50-4c76-8cbc-c7cfb9c526d8",
                                "sense_id": "f632291e-e7cd-3c4f-bbba-f33d14411554",
                                "text": "The Dominical Prayer, and the Apoſtolical Creed, (vvhereof there vvas ſuch a hot diſpute in our laſt converſation) are tvvo Acts tending to the ſame object of devotion, yet they differ in this, that vve conclude all in the firſt, and ourſelves only in the ſecond, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "00145735-bcdb-4246-8d44-74ddcac88971",
                                "sense_id": "f632291e-e7cd-3c4f-bbba-f33d14411554",
                                "text": "VVhereas 'tis clear, that Rome obſerved the firſt day of the vveek, becauſe 'tvvas the Dominical day, the day of our Lord's Reſurrection; vvhereas the proper Paſchal-day vvas tvvo or three days before the Lords day: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8dcb8a20-e96a-4b2a-9f66-1cb1cd4da528",
                                "sense_id": "f632291e-e7cd-3c4f-bbba-f33d14411554",
                                "text": "[A]t the firſt Intervievv vvith Mrs. Heartfree, Mr. VVild had conceived that Paſſion, […] vvhich is indeed no other than that Friendſhip vvhich, after the Exerciſe of the Dominical Day is over, a luſty Divine is apt to conceive for the vvell-dreſt Sirloin, or handſome Buttock, vvhich the vvell-edified 'Squire, in Gratitude, ſets before him, and vvhich, ſo violent is his Love, he is deſirous to devour."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac3ab7ca-9c21-3877-92bf-36b090c97506",
                        "entry_id": "46cadc45-63ea-3c6a-9768-6f09e06a878c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to the Lord's Day, Sunday."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75dd12b2-a202-4cf2-ab64-366a55880ca4",
                                "sense_id": "ac3ab7ca-9c21-3877-92bf-36b090c97506",
                                "text": "And vvho knovvs not the ſuperſtitious rigor of his Sundays Chapel, and the licentious remiſſneſs of his Sundays Theater; accompanied vvith that reverend Statute for Dominical Jigs and Maypoles, publiſht in his ovvn Name, and deriv'd from the example of his Father James."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "abeac177-41b0-3165-9e0d-640bdec1b7b9",
                        "entry_id": "46cadc45-63ea-3c6a-9768-6f09e06a878c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to the ancient system of dominical letters, used for determining Sundays (particularly Easter Sunday) in any given year.",
                            "Of printed text: in a large size."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "historical",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "943da50a-c086-4f5c-99d5-90242e781678",
                                "sense_id": "abeac177-41b0-3165-9e0d-640bdec1b7b9",
                                "text": "I haue compoſde a Dictionary, in vvhich / He is inſtructed, hovv, vvhen, and to vvhom / To be proud or humble; at vvhat times of the yeare / He may do a good deed for it ſelfe, and that is / VVrit in Dominicall letters, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45726fa4-846e-4090-87ea-bc610e2007b2",
                                "sense_id": "abeac177-41b0-3165-9e0d-640bdec1b7b9",
                                "text": "[S]uch obſerved that our Fights of greateſt importance vvere fought on the Lords day, As the Fight at Edgehill, Nevvbury, &c. as pointing at our ſin in the puniſhment, and Gods vvrath vvas vvritten in Dominical letters: […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78c17cfa-f82f-3db0-a154-be5e7a6fc43e",
                        "entry_id": "46cadc45-63ea-3c6a-9768-6f09e06a878c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to the ancient system of dominical letters, used for determining Sundays (particularly Easter Sunday) in any given year.",
                            "Red, ruddy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "historical",
                            "not-comparable",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa8b825b-230c-4126-b122-014756a4cf88",
                                "sense_id": "78c17cfa-f82f-3db0-a154-be5e7a6fc43e",
                                "text": "[T]hese nails that by good token have not been pared since eighty-eight, should have scratched your face till it had been a dominical one, and as full of red letters as any Pond's Almanac in Christendom."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
